# e2e/scenarios-index.md is generated by scripts/scenarios-index.mjs, never hand-written. Its own
# byte-exact output is the source of truth: PR-API-07 (e2e/process/process.api.spec.ts) compares the
# file on disk against `node scripts/scenarios-index.mjs check` verbatim. Prettier reformats markdown
# table column padding, which would make that comparison fail on every commit that runs `format` —
# not a bug in the generator, a genuine conflict between two formatters wanting the same bytes. Do
# not remove this line without also changing PR-API-07 to tolerate Prettier's formatting.
e2e/scenarios-index.md

# A research probe file quotes a command and its literal output as the citation research-protocol
# requires. Prettier's default embeddedLanguageFormatting reformats the contents of tagged code
# fences — rewriting quotes, exploding single-line CSS, re-indenting a package.json exports map —
# so the fenced block stops being the verbatim bytes the run produced. A rewritten quote is no
# longer evidence, it is a paraphrase that happens to look like one. Every change folder has one of
# these.
docs/plans/*/research/probes.md

# docs/profiling/verdicts/ holds each gate reviewer's final report exactly as the SubagentStop hook
# (scripts/save-verdict.mjs) captured it. Like probes.md, it is verbatim evidence: a reformatted
# table or a re-wrapped finding is a paraphrase, and `pnpm verdicts:report` parses the block by its
# literal shape. The files are never hand-written, so there is nothing to keep tidy.
docs/profiling/verdicts/

# docs/board.html is generated by scripts/board.mjs on every commit (.husky/pre-commit, CH-040);
# its bytes are the generator's, not Prettier's.
docs/board.html
